<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs actual Wednesday 113,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs actual Wednesday 113,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said Wednesday's actual receipts 113,000 head. Opening trade was not well established. Early sales of barrows and gilts $0.50 higher than mid-session Wednesday. Top $53.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>US 1-3 46-49% Carcass Base Lean*   Country	Plants</p>
<p>	220-260 lbs		 51.00 -52.00	52.00 -53.00</p>
<p>few				   50.50  52.50	51.50  53.50</p>
<p>Sows - steady/up $2.00. Top $51.00.</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs.	    41.00 -44.00	43.00 -45.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.			44.00 -46.00	45.00 -46.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up			 48.00 -50.00	49.00 -51.00</p>
<p>*note - prices were 220-280 lbs represent hogs averaging 73 to 74 pct carcasses yields with mostly 1 to 1.25 inches of last rib back fact and 47 to 48 lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
</text>
